        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Plan on roughly $10,000 to $16,000 for a typical Generac 22kW installed on natural gas, more with propane, long runs or panel work, plus a few hundred dollars a year in upkeep. The generator is less than half of that; the installation is where quotes differ and where careful shopping saves money.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Get three itemized quotes, insist on a real load calculation, place the unit as close to the meter and panel as code allows, and consider load management before upsizing. If outages in your area are short and rare, a portable with an interlock or a battery station may be the smarter spend.
          </p>
